            <div xml:id="d100">

                <pb facs="0204" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Secretary’s Daily Meetings, lot 58 D 609</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Executive Secretary
                        (McWilliams)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1952-04-25">April 25,
                            1952</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Summary of Meeting with the Secretary.</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>Participants:</label>
                    <item>Mr. Acheson</item>
                    <item>Mr. Bruce</item>
                    <item>Mr. Matthews</item>
                    <item>Mr. Sargeant</item>
                    <item>Mr. Bohlen</item>
                    <item>Mr. McFall</item>
                    <item>Mr. Jessup</item>
                    <item>Mr. Howe</item>
                    <item>Mr. Nitze</item>
                    <item>Mr. McWilliams</item>
                    <item>Mr. Battle</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#flush">Item 1. <hi rendition="#italic">Korean Briefing</hi></p>
                <p>Mr. Howe gave the briefing.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Item 2. <hi rendition="#italic">Negotiations in Korea</hi></p>
                <p>Practically the entire meeting was spent in a discussion of the current state of
                    negotiations in Korea and the steps which should be taken to prepare American
                    and world opinion for the decisive turn of events which seems to be at hand. The
                    two main questions at issue are: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Should we make a public statement in respect to the build-up of
                            Communist strength and the probability of a heavy resumption of
                            hostilities. General Smith is anxious that something be done on
                            this.</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>Should we have congressional consultations at this stage of the
                            negotiations.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <pb facs="0205" n="171" xml:id="pg171"/>
                <p>The matter was left that Messrs. Matthews, Sargeant, Bohlen, McFall and Johnson
                    would get together this morning and try to outline the course of action which
                    should be taken during the next 48 hours.</p>
                <p>[Here follows a summary of discussions on Trieste and the Varvaressos report on
                    Greece. For documentation on these two issues, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1952-54v08">volume VIII</ref>.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. McWilliams</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
